[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3619559928","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3619559928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3619559928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xvhn4","user":{"login":"DarkKilauea","id":1929107,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjkxMDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1929107?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea","html_url":"https://github.com/DarkKilauea","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarkKilauea/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-06T05:36:35Z","updated_at":"2025-12-06T05:36:35Z","body":"I tested this with #94496 to see if it fixed the sun looking too dim on HDR displays. It does appear to solve that issue, so I think this PR may be important to merge in 4.7 with the rest of the HDR related PRs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3619559928/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837031555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3837031555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3837031555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ktHSD","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T18:50:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T18:50:54Z","body":"Physically speaking, there are problems with add or mix. Neither of these are good at approximating the interaction between a sky's colour and the sun that is lighting it. The sun has a true colour that is effectively what we adapt to being \"white\" that is tinted towards red wavelengths because the blue wavelengths from the sun are scattered into the rest of the sky. So this means a white sun appears more redish (yellowish) and the sky appears blue instead of black or dark grey. This is not an additive process at all, unlike many other types of light interactions we're used to; it's more like a prism separating out light of different wavelengths.\r\n\r\nTo give control to artists, it makes sense to do something other than add blending so that the sun colour can be the sun colour, plain and simple, without needing to fight with how its blending with the sky. If you want a red sun, you can get a red sun, regardless of the sky, for example.\r\n\r\nOne consideration for the sun's intensity in procedural sky is to adjust it to be normalized to the effective `white` of the scene, as determined by `RendererEnvironmentStorage::environment_get_white(...)`. But this is a different behaviour that would prevent a non-bright sun.\r\n\r\nI don't quite understand the premultiplied alpha blending based on HSV just yet, so I'm somewhat curious to see what the math is on this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837031555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873203350","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3873203350","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3873203350,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m3GSW","user":{"login":"KeyboardDanni","id":34800072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODAwMDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34800072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni","html_url":"https://github.com/KeyboardDanni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KeyboardDanni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T18:16:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T18:16:10Z","body":"> To give control to artists, it makes sense to do something other than add blending so that the sun colour can be the sun colour, plain and simple, without needing to fight with how its blending with the sky. If you want a red sun, you can get a red sun, regardless of the sky, for example.\r\n\r\nThe main issue I see is that the sun's energy is also factored into this, with no way to work around it besides a custom shader. As an artist I'd expect a weaker sun to just become more faint, rather than turn black. For a day/night cycle you need to be able to fade the sun's energy so that the lighting and shadows don't suddenly disappear when the sun goes below the horizon (and keeping the sun on creates a bunch of issues since the world can't properly occlude it via shadowmapping).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873203350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873257998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3873257998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3873257998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7m3ToO","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T18:27:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T18:27:22Z","body":"Yep! Changing the blend mode of the sun is not the solution. Instead, the energy of the directional light should not affect the sun colour. I'm not sure exactly what the reasoning was to have the energy affect the colour, but I suspect the behaviour below energy values of `1.0` was not the purpose of this behaviour.\r\n\r\nBut doing an overhaul of the way that the sun is rendered is probably not trivial, given that Godot has shipped with the current behaviour for years and many games have been configured based on it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3873257998/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3930501894","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3930501894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3930501894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qRrMG","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T22:26:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T22:26:37Z","body":"> Instead, the energy of the directional light should not affect the sun colour. I'm not sure exactly what the reasoning was to have the energy affect the colour, but I suspect the behaviour below energy values of 1.0 was not the purpose of this behaviour\r\n\r\nWe could make energy values below `1.0` act like `1.0` for the purposes of sky rendering. On the other hand, this may not suffice to achieve good-looking day/night cycles on its own.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3930501894/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3953904631","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3953904631","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3953904631,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rq8v3","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T18:22:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T18:22:44Z","body":"> We could make energy values below `1.0` act like `1.0` for the purposes of sky rendering. On the other hand, this may not suffice to achieve good-looking day/night cycles on its own.\r\n\r\nThis would only affect the sun rendering, correct? If that's right then I think this is a reasonable patch to correct this obviously incorrect behaviour. Anything more than this I believe would be better suited with a complete overhaul of sun rendering in the procedural sky feature.\r\n\r\nThat's my thought anyway.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3953904631/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955387874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113292#issuecomment-3955387874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113292","id":3955387874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rwm3i","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T23:49:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T23:49:20Z","body":"> This would only affect the sun rendering, correct?\r\n\r\nYes, the light rendering would remain intact. I'll open a separate PR for this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955387874/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]